test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T18:41:20.5311515Z             "body": "This draft preserves original local stdio MCP and adds bounded batch/jobs, private profiles/artifacts, production packaging, lifecycle controls and fork-specific installation. Publishing remains disabled; release acceptance is blocked.\n\nCurrent candidate47d9c21 fixes a reproduced QA preservation defect: the installed journal smoke previously swallowed close errors and unconditionally deleted its separate journal directory after failed opens/assertions. It now removes only after acceptance/all closes succeed, retains failed or unconfirmed cases, and propagates close failures with the primary error. Bounded diagnostics report workspace/client counts without journal contents. Original MCP fixture teardown also emits bounded final tool progress and EOF/byte/overflow state when only teardown fails; no extra wait or SDK limit change.\n\nActual-worker baseline Node22 reproduces deletion after init timeout and swallowed close error after two real worker exits. Fixed negative/positive cases verify retention/removal on Node22/24; final registered-client scalar cases pass. Fresh production-package checks pass, as do typecheck/lint/actionlint (shellcheck/pyflakes disabled). Healthy stdio calibration passes; existing1,048,577-byte producer still fails and verifies bounded failure metadata. Negative calibrations are not native/production passes.297-file dry package excludes QA/actions/jobs fixtures/evidence.\n\nJournal version/project/key identity is revalidated under the existing schema write lock; all12 real second-connection race checks pass in native91 and92. Shared Ubuntu source preparation now covers all five configured host browser-install paths. Native92 executes six Linux instances across four normal paths, each changing one targeted file with no matched Azure URI remaining; opt-in functional soak is unexecuted. No timing guarantee or Docker image source rewrite claimed.\n\nLatest completed native92 at6884c4a: [batch](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39818353567)1422 pass/3 fail; [original](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39818353471)577/4; completed summaries1999/7. Windows main unexecuted after package verification fails. Other four package steps pass; all component jobs incl12 race cases pass. Linux main207/211/211 pass; Mac208/3. All17 logs recovered; one empty stream-error read retained plus successful ordinary retry; no cancellation request.\n\nWindows installed original/profile/batch/jobs/controller checks pass before journal init fails with rpc_timeout/init, last phase directory, worker exit unconfirmed. Layout probe is skipped for unconfirmed prior cleanup. Outer install workspace is preserved, but the old inner-fixture retention gap cannot be retroactively repaired. New preservation code does not fix latency, identify the blocking operation, retry, signal from hints, clear leases or confirm that old exit.\n\nActual Codex1k passes all3 OSs (Linux37.200s/Win38.537s/Mac79.429s, model0/owned0). Separate Mac main raw982/SDK950/sync986 time out; SDK/sync cleanup confirmed, raw reports no cleanup failure. Separate server/pipe1k controls pass118.247s/110.323s, owned0. These do not clear native89 Windows CRASHED750, native87 scoped observation or historical136/142 birth-record gaps.\n\nOriginal failures: Windows WebKit WAV/VP9 readiness, legacy headed Firefox context timeout, Mac Chrome advanced fixture stderr EOF unconfirmed. All12 independent trace/PDF/large-DOM cases pass. Mac strict video cases pass; actual-gray gate is ineligible, so no fresh controls/independent decoder probes run. Native90 gray cause remains unresolved, with no speculative encoder patch or assertion waiver.\n\nG00–G18 in docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md and docs/evidence/native92-summary.json retain complete scopes, logs and pending cases. No merge, publication, unsafe replay, default transport change or ownership-debt clearance.",
